---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SkillsToolkit from '../components/SkillsToolkit.astro';
---

<Layout title="Experience" description="Professional experience spanning DC CAP Scholars, Common App, University of Virginia, and Teach For America. PhD, MPP, IES Fellow.">
	<main class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-16 lg:px-8 lg:py-24">
		<h1
			class="mb-16 text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight text-neutral-900 sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl"
		>
			Experience
		</h1>

		<div class="space-y-20">
			<section>
				<h2
					class="mb-12 text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 sm:text-3xl lg:text-4xl"
				>
					Professional Experience
				</h2>

				<div class="space-y-16 border-l-2 border-neutral-200 pl-16 sm:pl-28">
					<div class="relative">
						<div
							class="absolute -left-[11px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full border-2 border-white bg-primary"
						></div>
						<div class="pl-6">
							<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 sm:text-2xl">
								Chief Strategy and Analytics Officer | DC CAP
							</h3>
							<p class="mt-1 text-base text-neutral-600">July 2023 – Present | Washington, DC</p>

							<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Executive Leadership:</strong> Member of the Senior Leadership Team reporting to the CEO. Drive the organization's "2050 Moonshot" strategy (80% college completion) across ~800 scholars. Pivoted DC CAP to a regional partnership model after a rigorous program evaluation on arrival — now Pillar 1 of the FY26–28 strategy. The partner program now sustains 85–90% first-year retention across multiple cohorts, with graduation rates of 75–95% at established partners.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Innovation + Fundraising:</strong> Launched DC CAP's Innovation Hub on a $600K KPMG AI Impact Initiative grant, the organization's largest AI investment. The Hub houses the AI Governance Framework, the Career Pathway Intelligence Platform (launching October 2026), and our career-connected learning roadmap. Instrumental in $50M+ in philanthropic commitments since joining, including MacKenzie Scott / Yield Giving.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Organizational Health:</strong> Oversee Student Success, University Partnerships, GEAR UP, Innovation, and Data & Technology units. Build the analytics, evaluation, and storytelling infrastructure that anchors the annual fundraising model.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Change Management:</strong> Lead the digital transformation roadmap. Designed the AI Governance Framework and run our 60-day AI pilot (nine staff, three units, April–June 2026). Application process compressed from ~10 staff at 20+ hours/week to 1 staff at 3–5 hours/week. Coach administrative load reduced from ~60% of time to under 10%.
								</p>

							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="relative">
						<div
							class="absolute -left-[11px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full border-2 border-white bg-primary"
						></div>
						<div class="pl-6">
							<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 sm:text-2xl">
								Senior Manager of Research & Analytics | Common App
							</h3>
							<p class="mt-1 text-base text-neutral-600">Oct 2020 – July 2023 | Remote</p>

							<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Founding Team Member:</strong> Second member of the founding research function at Common App, the largest college application dataset in the United States. Defined the data environment, technical stack, research agenda, and data sharing policies.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">External Relations:</strong> Primary spokesperson for data insights, representing the organization to national media (NYT, Bloomberg) and the Board of Directors.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Strategic Partnerships:</strong> Negotiated and managed research collaborations and data-sharing protocols with leading universities. Resulting work was profiled at NBER, Brookings, the Association for Education Finance and Policy (AEFP), and the EdWorkingPapers Series at Brown University's Annenberg Institute. Led randomized control trials on direct admissions and text-message information campaigns.
								</p>

							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="relative">
						<div
							class="absolute -left-[11px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full border-2 border-white bg-primary"
						></div>
						<div class="pl-6">
							<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 sm:text-2xl">
								IES Predoctoral Fellow, Educational Policy Studies | University of Virginia
							</h3>
							<p class="mt-1 text-base text-neutral-600">Aug 2015 – Aug 2020 | Charlottesville, VA</p>

							<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">UVA–Louisiana Department of Education Partnership:</strong> Lead researcher on a multi-year research-practice partnership with the Louisiana Department of Education on policy and accountability systems research (2017–2020). Worked directly with state policymakers and district leaders during a statewide policy rollout on accountability design.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Published Research:</strong> The partnership produced peer-reviewed publications on policy implementation and program quality. The first statewide longitudinal study of early-childhood program quality improvement under a mandatory QRIS appeared in AERA Open and ECRQ, alongside additional accountability-policy research and a policy brief.
								</p>

							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="relative">
						<div
							class="absolute -left-[11px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full border-2 border-white bg-primary"
						></div>
						<div class="pl-6">
							<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 sm:text-2xl">
								Associate Editor | Peabody Journal of Education
							</h3>
							<p class="mt-1 text-base text-neutral-600">2013 – 2015 | Nashville, TN</p>
							<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
								<p>
									Managed editorial operations, review pipelines, and production scheduling for one
									of the nation's oldest education policy journals while completing MPP coursework.
								</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="relative">
						<div
							class="absolute -left-[11px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full border-2 border-white bg-primary"
						></div>
						<div class="pl-6">
							<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 sm:text-2xl">
								Corps Member | Teach For America
							</h3>
							<p class="mt-1 text-base text-neutral-600">2011 – 2013 | South Louisiana</p>
							<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
								<p>
									Led large achievement gains in elementary school turnaround environment (95th
									percentile value-added scores). Selected as regional winner of the Excellence in
									Teaching Award.
								</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2
					class="mb-12 text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 sm:text-3xl lg:text-4xl"
				>
					Education
				</h2>
				<div class="space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
					<div class="border-l-2 border-neutral-100 pl-6">
						<strong class="block text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900"
							>Ph.D., Educational Policy Studies</strong
						>
						<span class="text-neutral-600">University of Virginia (IES Fellow) | 2020</span>
					</div>
					<div class="border-l-2 border-neutral-100 pl-6">
						<strong class="block text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900">M.P.P., Public Policy</strong>
						<span class="text-neutral-600">Vanderbilt University (Peabody Honors Scholar) | 2015</span>
					</div>
					<div class="border-l-2 border-neutral-100 pl-6">
						<strong class="block text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900">B.A., History</strong>
						<span class="text-neutral-600">Tulane University | 2011</span>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>
		</div>
	</main>
	<SkillsToolkit />
</Layout>
